From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <rainb@tfwno.gf>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:49:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Do not jump over initialized declarations

C++ does not allow a goto to skip the initialization of a variable that
is still in scope at the label. MSVC accepts it, GCC rejects it. Declare
those variables first and assign them separately; the error paths never
read them, so the behavior is unchanged.
---
 Driver.cpp       | 21 ++++++++++++++-------
 adapter.cpp      |  9 ++++++---
 control.cpp      |  3 ++-
 crypto.cpp       |  9 ++++++---
 crypto_epoch.cpp | 15 ++++++++++-----
 peer.cpp         | 27 ++++++++++++++++++---------
 socket.cpp       | 15 ++++++++++-----
 trie.cpp         |  6 ++++--
 8 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

